  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of Education obligated $59.1M in FY2027 to date across 126 awards. The Department of Education reported average award size of $469K and obligations fell 97.9% year over year. The Department of Education spent far less in FY27 to date than in prior full fiscal years, which ranged from $2.4B to $2.8B. The Department of Education concentrated FY2027 to date obligations in Computer Systems Design Services ($31.4M) and Research and Development in the Social Sciences and Humanities ($24.9M), with smaller allocations to Custom Computer Programming Services ($11.9M) and several other service categories. The Department of Education directed the largest shares of FY2027 to date obligations to GENERAL DYNAMICS INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY, INC. ($18.9M), EDUCATIONAL TESTING SERVICE ($14.4M), and T-REX SOLUTIONS LLC ($12.6M). The Department of Education FY27 to date totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date obligations only.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How does current-year spending compare to prior years?",
        "body": "The Department of Education obligated $59.1M in FY2027 to date, versus full-year totals of $2.4B, $2.4B, $2.7B, $2.5B, and $2.8B for FY22 through FY26. The Department of Education reported obligations fell 97.9% year over year. The Department of Education FY27 figure is a fiscal year to date total and is much smaller than prior full-year obligations."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What are the biggest categories and vendors this year?",
        "body": "Computer Systems Design Services is the largest category at $31.4M, followed by Research and Development in the Social Sciences and Humanities at $24.9M and Custom Computer Programming Services at $11.9M. GENERAL DYNAMICS INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY, INC. is the largest vendor at $18.9M, followed by EDUCATIONAL TESTING SERVICE at $14.4M and T-REX SOLUTIONS LLC at $12.6M."
      }
    ]
